{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.CategoricalNeutralitySaturatedShells","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.CategoricalNeutralitySaturatedShells","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Set.Finite.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Common.MagicNumbers"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_iter_two_sided_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_iter_two_sided_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L113-L130","doc":"Two-sided iteration: `fullTwist^a · Φ_n · fullTwist^b = Φ_n`\nfor any `a, b : ℕ` at a saturated level. The full-twist's\ndiscrete `ℕ × ℕ`-monoid action on `Φ_n` factors through the\ntrivial representation under the saturated-shell conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_iter_neutral_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_iter_neutral_right","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L97-L111","doc":"The right-iteration analogue of `fullTwist_iter_neutral`:\n`Φ_n · fullTwist^k = Φ_n` for any `k : ℕ`. Proves directly by\ninduction using `neutrality_right`, mirroring the left-side\nproof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_iter_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_iter_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L83-L95","doc":"Conditional theorem: at a saturated level, two applications of\nthe full-twist still leave `Φ_n` invariant — the discrete\n`ℤ`-action of the full-twist factors through the trivial\nrepresentation on `Φ_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.fullTwist_commutes","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L75-L81","doc":"Conditional theorem: under the saturated-shell conjecture, the\nfull-twist commutes with `Φ_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.neutrality_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.neutrality_right","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The asserted neutrality: full-twist commutes-and-fixes `Φ_n`\nfrom the right. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.neutrality_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.neutrality_left","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The asserted neutrality: full-twist commutes-and-fixes `Φ_n`\nfrom the left. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.saturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.saturated","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The level `n` lies in the magic set (precondition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.toMassEndoModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture.toMassEndoModule","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L65-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.SaturatedShellConjecture","kind":"class","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L57-L73","doc":"The conjecture, encoded as a class.\n\nA `SaturatedShellConjecture n` instance asserts that, at the\nsaturated level `n`, the full-twist `Δ_n²` acts trivially on\n`Φ_n` in the endomorphism algebra `Endo n`. The unproved input\nis the existence of the instance; downstream conditional\ntheorems are then fully verified by Lean. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells","label":"prop:categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.phi","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The categorical mass endomorphism `Φ_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.fullTwist","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The image of the full-twist `Δ_n²` in `Endo`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.endoMonoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.endoMonoid","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Endomorphism algebras are monoids (composition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.Endo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.Endo","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The endomorphism algebra at level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.MassEndoModule","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L36-L53","doc":"The mass-endomorphism module at level `n`, abstracted: any type\nwith a designated full-twist action and a designated mass\nendomorphism. The conjecture below asks whether the latter is\nfixed by the former at saturated levels.\n\nConcretely, in the QOU substrate `Endo n` will be instantiated\nas `End (A^⊗n)` in the rigid braided monoidal category `C`, the\n`fullTwist` is the central element `Δ_n²`, and `phi` is the\nglobal section of the mass functor at level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.Saturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.Saturated","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ShellNeutrality.magicSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ShellNeutrality.magicSet","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0}]}